text:
Sure! Here's a simple example using HTML and JavaScript to create a colorful website with real jokes:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f9f9f9;
            color: #333;
            text-align: center;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }
        header {
            background-color: #4CAF50;
            color: white;
            padding: 15px 0;
            border-bottom: 3px solid #388E3C;
        }
        .container {
            background: white;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
            margin: 20px auto;
            max-width: 600px;
        }
        .joke {
            background-color: #ffe6e6;
            padding: 10px;
            border-radius: 4px;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="joke" id="joke1">
            <h2>Really Funny Joke 1</h2>
            <p>Push 18 to reveal punchline</p>
            <button onclick="revealPunchline('joke1')">Reveal Punchline</button>
        </div>
        <div class="joke" id="joke2">
            <h2>Same But Joke 2</h2>
            <p>Push to reveal punchline</p>
            <button onclick="revealPunchline('joke2')">Reveal Punchline</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        function revealPunchline(jokeId) {
            document.getElementById(jokeId).classList.toggle('revealed');
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

